 should be  focusing on the  featured section the about you section  because the featured section will uh  will include all the laurels all the  achievements that she has had in the  past so it will showcase all those  things to the potential recruiter plus  about you is again the entire journey  the entire uh career trajectories the  various roles that she has had and now  she's looking for a better opportunity  perhaps now she is looking because of  her skill sets she she feels that she  can be offered another opportunity or a  better opportunity so she should keep  that in mind and  write the about you or the summary  section so these are the things that she  can you know keep  keep all the nine sections at an optimum  when she is looking for a career switch  this is what can be done  okay  um we have one last question before we  have to move on  and then that is we've got a number of  people who have asked about specific  career  or industries and domains  and um do you have advice for how  somebody  should brand themselves within their  particular industry whether it's uh  whether it's the  technology industry or education  industry  or  even a question came in from someone who  wants to be an animator  how would you address that  yeah okay so the first thing as i said  whichever industry you are from  learn to be an expert at your job you  know you have to be an expert in your  niche you have to be an expert in that  industry which you belong to because  there are so many people who have these  technical skills these four skills what  is that thing what is that exclusive  thing that sets you apart from the  others so you need to focus on that and  you need to think in a different manner  think in an innovative manner to  distinguish yourself to differentiate  yourself from the other so this is the  first thing that you of course you need  to be an expert you need to have an  expertise in your industry but also make  yourself more visible also uh provide  enough value you know value is very very  important because people who have the  expertise if they do not provide that  same value to others then the whole game  is lost so personal branding itself  means the kind of value and experience  you can provide to others so that they  think you are an expert  and you can project yourself as an  expert in this manner so provide enough  value and of course be an expert in your  field and you will have an awesome  personal brand for yourself  i'm going to put into the chat window  now a number of uh  resources that  seema has shared which are  her contact information  her linkedin profile and a link to her  book  on career skills for professional  success  and  i'm going to move on to the last part  close out the webinar so thank you  everybody for your patience and for  being here  thank you very much for um  to seema for for being here  and thank you stuart thank you everyone  for joining  yeah  let me move on  we have a final poll  which asks  if you are involved in technology and  are looking to develop technology skills  which of those skills are you most  interested in learning  you can pick one or more  and the second part of the question is  very important  when will you start  that learning process  we always get a number of questions  about attendance certificates for these  webinars  but we also  want to ask you about earning actual  certificates for skills that you've  acquired  so  when are you interested in  starting that and what skills are you  looking to develop  and we've got about 10 more seconds on  the poll  and we'll close it in two more seconds  here  and  here are the results  so the most popular categories are  business and project management data  science  and digital marketing  and it's good to see that about  40 of the audience is interested in  getting started right away with another  20 or so looking to start  soon within the next three months so  with that said i'm just going to point  out  a resource that simply learn offers  which is called the skill up program and  the skill up program is free  it allows you to study  in these different  skill domains  and  you can earn certificates for completing  these self-study courses  these are sort of introductory to the  more  involved courses that we offer that  include  live virtual classrooms and hands-on  labs and that type of thing but these  skill up courses are  self-study video and  they're free you can do them on your own  schedule and they do offer completion  certificates that you can add to your  linkedin profile so  i'm going to put that information in the  chat now with the link to our  skill up  home page  and  last item i'd like to mention that we  have two more webinars this week  so if you are interested in these topics  the first one is  product management the second one is a  technical master class for digital  marketers  and  i'll put those in the chat as well  and they'll be held at the same time of  day which is 9 p.m india time and  8 30 pacific 11 30 eastern  in north america  and  with that said  i invite all of you to connect with us  on our  social media channels  at simplylearn on facebook and twitter  simply learn on linkedin  again thank you so much  to sema for being here and thank you to  everyone in the audience being here  today  all right  and that concludes our webinar  you
 

